{
  "_comment": [
    "Agent config for the REAL acquisition laptop. Copy to the station as",
    "/etc/agent/station.json (or anywhere, and point AGENT_CONFIG at it):",
    "",
    "  scp deploy/station-dob.json.example ionouser@<laptop>:~/agent.json",
    "  # edit server_url (NOT token -- see below), then:",
    "  cd ~/chirpsounder2 && source .venv38/bin/activate",
    "  AGENT_TOKEN=... AGENT_CONFIG=~/agent.json python -m services.agent health",
    "",
    "The agent is Python 3.8 clean, so the station's .venv38 runs it. It needs",
    "the ionograms-handler repo on PYTHONPATH for `services` and `muf`.",
    "",
    "server_url must be reachable FROM the laptop. Health is pushed and",
    "commands are pulled, so the laptop only ever makes outbound connections",
    "and never needs an inbound port -- but the server does. See",
    "deploy/README.md for the two network cases.",
    "",
    "Leave \"token\" empty and pass the secret as AGENT_TOKEN in the unit's",
    "environment instead. It overrides this field, and keeps the shared secret",
    "out of a file that gets copied around and backed up. The unit reads",
    "/etc/default/chirp-agent (root-owned, 0600); its one line is",
    "AGENT_TOKEN=<the server's CONTROL_TOKEN>.",
    "",
    "This laptop needs no deploy/.env -- that file configures Compose on the",
    "work server, and is host-specific besides. This file plus that one-line",
    "token file is the whole of the station's configuration."
  ],

  "_station_comment": [
    "The site is Yoshkar-Ola (56.38N 47.53E), not Dombas. `my_station.ini`",
    "wrote station_name=DOB from the start and this file copied it, so every",
    "product, filename and database row up to 2026-08-16 carries a code that",
    "belongs to a different site 2400 km away. muf/stations.py resolves DOB to",
    "62.073N 9.111E, which is where every wrong path length came from.",
    "",
    "This field labels HEALTH AND COMMANDS ONLY. The receiver name on a",
    "sounding comes from the product file, written by chirpsounder2 out of",
    "my_station.ini. Change one without the other and the console splits the",
    "station in two: a new name with live metrics and no data, an old name",
    "with every sounding ever ingested and no agent."
  ],
  "station": "Yoshkar-Ola",
  "server_url": "http://<work-pc-lan-ip>:8002",
  "token": "",
  "push_interval_s": 60,

  "chirp_config": "/home/ionouser/chirpsounder2/my_station.ini",

  "_output_dir_comment": [
    "The BOOT SSD, and this file said /media/ionouser/DATA3/ionozond_data2",
    "until 2026-08-18 while the station wrote here. DATA3 is a USB-attached",
    "NTFS volume served by a `mount.ntfs` FUSE daemon measured at 8.2% CPU on",
    "a host that cannot spare it -- writing products there costs the recorder",
    "samples. The trade is 256 GB of headroom instead of 928 GB, which is why",
    "chirp-archive-prune exists.",
    "",
    "Getting this wrong is quiet, and it is quiet in three separate places at",
    "once: newest_product_age_s reports `no such directory` or `no recent",
    "product` for a recorder that is producing normally, the station preview",
    "finds nothing to encode and the console says the agent must be too old,",
    "and chirp-archive-sync mirrors an empty tree and reports success. Nothing",
    "in that list looks like a wrong path.",
    "",
    "Three places, one path: here, ARCHIVE_LOCAL in chirp-archive-sync.service",
    "and ARCHIVE_LOCAL in chirp-archive-prune.service. A test pins all three",
    "together. The authority above all of them is `output_dir` in",
    "my_station.ini -- that is what chirpsounder2 actually obeys; these three",
    "only describe it."
  ],
  "output_dir": "/home/ionouser/ionozond_data2",

  "_ringbuffer_unit_comment": [
    "Read only for the -z size in its ExecStart, and only to judge",
    "ringbuffer_free_fraction. The ring is SUPPOSED to sit at its cap --",
    "14000MB of a 16.8 GB tmpfs here, so 16.7% free is what a perfectly",
    "trimming buffer looks like, against a flat 15% floor. 1.7 points. The",
    "threshold and the buffer size were set independently and nearly",
    "collide, so the station read as one bad minute from red, forever.",
    "",
    "With the cap known, full-to-cap is 100% of designed headroom and green;",
    "anything eating that headroom is not. Set \"\" on a station whose",
    "ringbuffer is started by a script -- the metric then falls back to the",
    "flat floor and says in its detail that it did.",
    "",
    "It cannot be an early warning and does not pretend to be: at 25 MS/s",
    "the recorder writes 100 MB/s, so a dead trimmer crosses 2.8 GB of",
    "headroom in 28 seconds, inside one push interval. The leading",
    "indicator is the bounded `% size` line in journalctl -u",
    "chirp-ringbuffer, which stops or reaches 100%."
  ],
  "ringbuffer_dir": "/dev/shm/hf25",
  "ringbuffer_unit": "chirp-ringbuffer.service",

  "_units_comment": [
    "EMPTY ON PURPOSE, while DOB is still run by dombas.sh.",
    "",
    "`systemctl is-active` is the supervision boundary, and dombas.sh is not",
    "systemd: it owns rx_uhd_ext_gps and `drf ringbuffer` as its own children.",
    "So is-active answers `inactive` for a recorder that is running, health.py",
    "reads that as a definite failure, and the station reports UNHEALTHY while",
    "it acquires perfectly well. Eleven false reds is worse than no unit",
    "metrics: it is exactly how a status column stops being read.",
    "",
    "What still watches the station without them: newest_product_age_s,",
    "ringbuffer_free_fraction, sample_rate_hz and system_clock_s. Those are",
    "the ones that caught the real outage anyway -- /dev/shm at 100% and an",
    "epoch of 2021 -- because they measure the acquisition rather than the",
    "supervisor.",
    "",
    "`target` is empty for the same reason, and that one is a safety",
    "interlock: `systemctl restart chirp.target` on a script-run station does",
    "not restart what is running, it starts a SECOND recorder against the same",
    "USRP, and two streamers means power-cycling the radio by hand. With no",
    "target the agent refuses the verb and says why.",
    "",
    "Move to _units_when_migrated below once dombas.sh is retired and the",
    "units in services/agent/systemd/ are what actually starts acquisition.",
    "Do not enable both."
  ],
  "units": [],
  "target": "",

  "_units_when_migrated": [
    "Every unit whose death should be visible, once systemd is the supervisor.",
    "A process missing from this list cannot be reported unhealthy, and",
    "chirp-ringbuffer is the reason that matters: nothing trimmed /dev/shm, it",
    "sat at 100%, the recording developed holes, and every other process",
    "stayed green for two days. Drop chirp-timings when not in serendipitous",
    "mode -- it produces the par-*.h5 that only that mode consumes.",
    "",
    "Set `target` to chirp.target at the same time, never before: the target",
    "is what start/stop/restart act on.",
    "",
    "NO chirp-digisonde@ INSTANCE BELONGS IN THIS LIST, and none should be",
    "enabled. This list used to name four of them and that was wrong: patch",
    "0007 removed the digisonde receivers from dombas.sh because they are the",
    "cause of the 45% sample loss -- receiving five of them off air cost ~969",
    "dropped events/s and ~65,000 RcvbufErrors/s, and stopping them took the",
    "recorder to zero drops over a full hour. They are ringbuffer consumers at",
    "25 MS/s, not downloaders, and ~3.4 cores of an 8-core budget that the",
    "unavoidable pipeline already spends 4.4 of. Listing them here is how they",
    "come back: the list is copied into agent.json and then read as the set of",
    "units to enable. On 2026-08-16 exactly that happened.",
    "",
    "`optional_units` defaults to [\"chirp-digisonde@\"] so that a station",
    "which still has one of them listed reports its state as unknown rather",
    "than as a failure -- a stopped one is the correct state here, and four",
    "permanent reds are how a status column stops being read. That default is",
    "a safety net for a config that has not been cleaned up yet, not a licence",
    "to list them: an exempt unit is still a ringbuffer consumer when it runs.",
    "Set \"optional_units\": [] on a receiver that really does depend on one.",
    "",
    "chirp-rx.service",
    "chirp-ringbuffer.service",
    "chirp-detect.service",
    "chirp-timings.service",
    "chirp-ionograms.service",
    "chirp-metadata.service"
  ],

  "_chirp_sync_comment": [
    "chirp-sync.service is DELIBERATELY absent from the list above, and was",
    "removed from it on 2026-09-14 after being watched for weeks as a",
    "permanent red.",
    "",
    "It uploads dashboard images, gated on `copy_to_server` in my_station.ini",
    "-- and that key is false here on purpose: it also gates seven blocking",
    "60 s POSTs to juha.no, one of them inside calc_ionograms.py:438, which",
    "is the 8.37% sounding loss of BACKLOG sec. 3. See",
    "docs/chirpsounder2-config.md.",
    "",
    "With the key false the script prints `Copy to server disabled in",
    "configuration. Exiting` and exits 0 -- which Restart=always retries",
    "every 60 s forever, so the unit reports `activating` (SubState",
    "auto-restart) and health reads it as a failure. Disabled instead, it",
    "reports `inactive`, which health also reads as a failure. There is no",
    "state in which watching it is informative while the feature is off.",
    "",
    "Add it back ONLY together with `copy_to_server = true` AND an",
    "Environment=IONOWEBSYNC_URL= that this network can actually reach. The",
    "ini key is global, so enabling it for the dashboard enables it for the",
    "deadline-critical caller too."
  ],

  "startup_grace_s": 300,
  "expected_sample_rate": 25000000,

  "_preview_comment": [
    "A thumbnail of the newest product from each transmitter, encoded here and",
    "pushed alongside the health report. It is the only thing in the console",
    "that shows what this laptop is receiving RIGHT NOW: the arrivals table",
    "measures the archive, which reaches the server on chirp-archive-sync's",
    "timer and is routinely hours behind.",
    "",
    "What it costs on this machine, measured on real DOB products: 2.5 ms for",
    "an ordinary one, 18 ms for a search-mode one, once per push -- under a",
    "tenth of a percent of one core -- and about 3 KB on the wire. Nothing is",
    "recomputed: a v2 .h5 holds the ionogram already, so this is a read, a",
    "decimation and a PNG. At most four products are decoded per pass.",
    "",
    "It needs numpy and h5py, which is why it runs under chirpsounder2's",
    ".venv38 and not the system python. Without them the agent says so in the",
    "pass log and reports health exactly as before -- the preview can never",
    "take the health push down with it.",
    "",
    "Set false to send none. preview_size is [frequencies, ranges]; larger",
    "only sends pixels the console throws away."
  ],
  "preview": true,
  "preview_size": [128, 96],

  "_reference_tx_comment": [
    "distance_km is Nicosia to THIS RECEIVER, and it was 3436.0 here until",
    "2026-08-16 -- the Nicosia->Dombas figure, on a receiver that is not in",
    "Dombas. solve_epoch_offset models tau = distance/c with no ionospheric",
    "hop, so the 848 km error came back as clock error: epoch_offset_s read",
    "-0.002108 s against a GPSDO-disciplined recorder, where 2.1 ms of real",
    "clock error is not available. 2587.83 km moved it to +0.000975 s, i.e.",
    "positive, which is the only sign an unmodelled hop excess can produce.",
    "That is the measurement that confirmed the site, not just the assertion.",
    "",
    "It sat 25 us inside the old symmetric abs(offset) < 1e-3 threshold and",
    "flapped red whenever the virtual height ran high, which was most nights.",
    "Settled 2026-09-14: the window is now asymmetric and geometric.",
    "",
    "Early is the tight side -- the solve models a straight ground line, so",
    "no real path arrives sooner and -0.5 ms is already a slow clock. Late",
    "gets max_hops x max_virtual_height_km of budget, 2.13 ms here, because",
    "reflecting off a layer a few hundred km up is what the model leaves",
    "out. +1.28 ms measured that evening is two hops at ~330 km.",
    "",
    "The host clock is NOT in this budget and does not need to be: the",
    "recorder sets its epoch from the GPSDO gps_time sensor on a PPS edge",
    "(patch 0001, which prints `[source: GPSDO gps_time]` on every start).",
    "Measured the same evening, the host clock was 0.77 ms fast and none of",
    "it reached a sample. If that line ever says `host clock` instead, the",
    "GPSDO did not lock and this budget is the wrong shape."
  ],
  "reference_tx": {
    "name": "cyprus1",
    "rate": 100000.0,
    "transmit_seconds": [235, 240, 245, 300],
    "distance_km": 2587.83,
    "cycle_s": 300.0,
    "window_s": 2.0,
    "max_hops": 2,
    "max_virtual_height_km": 450.0
  }
}
